=== CompletedOI.lean:171 def ReversibleRichness  HEADLINE
DOC 169: /-- **REVERSIBLE RICHNESS**: every available reversible transformation can be undone, and at
DOC 170: every level a passive drift with finitely many controls generates `su(D)`. -/
SIG 171: def ReversibleRichness : Prop :=
SIG 172:   (∀ (n : ℕ) (V : Matrix (Fin 2 × Fin n) (Fin 2 × Fin n) ℂ),
SIG 173:     T.availExt n Unit (fun _ => conjChannel V) → T.availExt n Unit (fun _ => conjChannel Vᴴ))
SIG 174:   ∧ ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ (G : Type) (H : Matrix (Fin 2 × Fin n) (Fin 2 × Fin n) ℂ)
SIG 175:       (U : G → Matrix (Fin 2 × Fin n) (Fin 2 × Fin n) ℂ),
SIG 176:       Hᴴ = H ∧ (∀ g, (U g)ᴴ * U g = 1) ∧ HControl H U
SIG 177:         ∧ (∀ t : ℝ, T.availExt n Unit (fun _ => conjChannel (flow H t)))
SIG 178:         ∧ (∀ g, T.availExt n Unit (fun _ => conjChannel (U g)))
