=== CompletedOI.lean:557 theorem oiCore_forward_redundancy  HEADLINE
DOC 553: /-- **THE FORWARD-REDUNDANCY AUDIT ENTRY**, in one place: containment holds, the core is redundant
DOC 554: in the forward direction, and the converse fails. The three together are the whole of what the
DOC 555: formalization supports about "QM and OI", and they are exactly what rules out reading the
DOC 556: containment as an explanatory necessity. -/
SIG 557: theorem oiCore_forward_redundancy :
SIG 558:     (∀ T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2), ExactAllFiniteEndomorphicQuantumOps T → OICore T)
SIG 559:     ∧ (∀ T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2),
SIG 560:         CompletedOI T ↔ PhysicalCompletionConditions T)
SIG 561:     ∧ (∃ T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2),
SIG 562:         OICore T ∧ ¬ ExactAllFiniteEndomorphicQuantumOps T) :=
