=== ImplementationLocality.lean:244 abbrev ImplementationClass
DOC 242: /-- An implementation class: at every finite carrier, which single operators are admissible
DOC 243: physical implementations. -/
SIG 244: abbrev ImplementationClass :=
SIG 245:   ∀ (S : Type) [Fintype S] [DecidableEq S], Matrix S S ℂ → Prop
=== ImplementationLocality.lean:250 def Realized
DOC 247: /-- An operation is BRANCH-REALIZED by a class when it is a finite sum of conjugations by
DOC 248: admissible operators. This is the comparison notion; the availability of a theory is generated
DOC 249: by `InstAvail` below. -/
SIG 250: def Realized (𝓘 : ImplementationClass) (S : Type) [Fintype S] [DecidableEq S]
SIG 251:     (Φ : Matrix S S ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix S S ℂ) : Prop :=
SIG 252:   ∃ (ι : Type) (_ : Fintype ι) (K : ι → Matrix S S ℂ),
SIG 253:     Φ = ∑ i, conjChannel (K i) ∧ ∀ i, 𝓘 S (K i)
=== ImplementationLocality.lean:256 def readProj
DOC 255: /-- The readout projector onto the register value `k` of the carrier `T × Fin m`. -/
SIG 256: def readProj (T : Type) [DecidableEq T] (m : ℕ) (k : Fin m) :
SIG 257:     Matrix (T × Fin m) (T × Fin m) ℂ :=
SIG 258:   Matrix.diagonal fun r => if r.2 = k then 1 else 0
=== ImplementationLocality.lean:268 inductive InstAvail  HEADLINE
DOC 260: /-- **INSTRUMENT REALIZATION.** A family of operations on the carrier `T` with outcomes `O` is
DOC 261: instrument-realized by the class `𝓘` when it is built from: one admissible isometric step;
DOC 262: the native Lüders readout of a register `T' × Fin m ≃ T` of the carrier, its projectors
DOC 263: admissible; classical coarse-graining of the outcome; sequential composition with
DOC 264: outcome-dependent continuation; and the discard of a uniformly attached ancilla of positive
DOC 265: size. There is no constructor taking a sum of admissible operators: the branches of a realized
DOC 266: family arise together as the outcomes of one protocol, and the uniformly weighted preparation
DOC 267: label is summed inside the discard and is never an outcome. -/
SIG 268: inductive InstAvail (𝓘 : ImplementationClass) :
SIG 269:     ∀ (T : Type) [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T] (O : Type) [Fintype O] [DecidableEq O],
SIG 270:       (O → Matrix T T ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix T T ℂ) → Prop
SIG 271:   | op {T : Type} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T] (K : Matrix T T ℂ) (hK : 𝓘 T K)
SIG 272:       (hiso : Kᴴ * K = 1) : InstAvail 𝓘 T Unit (fun _ => conjChannel K)
SIG 273:   | readout {T T' : Type} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T] [Fintype T'] [DecidableEq T'] {m : ℕ}
SIG 274:       (e : T' × Fin m ≃ T) (hP : ∀ k, 𝓘 T (Matrix.reindex e e (readProj T' m k))) :
SIG 275:       InstAvail 𝓘 T (Fin m) (fun k => conjChannel (Matrix.reindex e e (readProj T' m k)))
SIG 276:   | coarse {T : Type} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T] {O O' : Type} [Fintype O] [DecidableEq O]
SIG 277:       [Fintype O'] [DecidableEq O'] {F : O → Matrix T T ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix T T ℂ} (f : O → O')
SIG 278:       (h : InstAvail 𝓘 T O F) :
SIG 279:       InstAvail 𝓘 T O' (fun a => ∑ j ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun j => f j = a), F j)
SIG 280:   | bind {T : Type} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T] {O O' : Type} [Fintype O] [DecidableEq O]
SIG 281:       [Fintype O'] [DecidableEq O'] {F : O → Matrix T T ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix T T ℂ}
SIG 282:       {G : O → O' → Matrix T T ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix T T ℂ} (hF : InstAvail 𝓘 T O F)
SIG 283:       (hG : ∀ a, InstAvail 𝓘 T O' (G a)) :
SIG 284:       InstAvail 𝓘 T (O × O') (fun c => (G c.1 c.2).comp (F c.1))
SIG 285:   | discard {T : Type} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T] {m : ℕ} (hm : 0 < m) {O : Type} [Fintype O]
SIG 286:       [DecidableEq O]
SIG 287:       {F : O → Matrix (T × Fin m) (T × Fin m) ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix (T × Fin m) (T × Fin m) ℂ}
SIG 288:       (h : InstAvail 𝓘 (T × Fin m) O F) :
SIG 289:       InstAvail 𝓘 T O (fun a => discardWith (A := T) m (uniformAttach m) (F a))
=== ImplementationLocality.lean:295 theorem conjChannel_trace_iff
DOC 293: /-- A one-outcome conjugation preserves the trace exactly when its operator is an isometry: the
DOC 294: contractive-plus-normalized reading of a step is the isometric one. -/
SIG 295: theorem conjChannel_trace_iff {T : Type} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T] (K : Matrix T T ℂ) :
SIG 296:     (∀ X : Matrix T T ℂ, (conjChannel K X).trace = X.trace) ↔ Kᴴ * K = 1 := by
=== ImplementationLocality.lean:305 theorem instAvail_mono
SIG 305: theorem instAvail_mono {𝓙 : ImplementationClass}
SIG 306:     (hle : ∀ (S : Type) [Fintype S] [DecidableEq S] (K : Matrix S S ℂ), 𝓘 S K → 𝓙 S K)
SIG 307:     {T : Type} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T] {O : Type} [Fintype O] [DecidableEq O]
SIG 308:     {F : O → Matrix T T ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix T T ℂ} (h : InstAvail 𝓘 T O F) : InstAvail 𝓙 T O F := by
=== ImplementationLocality.lean:317 theorem instAvail_trace  HEADLINE
DOC 316: /-- **T1, THE TRACE**: an instrument-realized family preserves the trace in aggregate. -/
