=== PositiveReachability.lean:457 theorem exists_nested_spanning  HEADLINE
DOC 454: /-- **GREEDY PREFIXES.** Starting from any positive word `P` and any subspace `W` of the span, a
DOC 455: tuple `A` of positive words can be chosen so that `W` together with the directions of the nested
DOC 456: prefixes `P A_0 ⋯ A_j` spans the whole positive orbit span. Induction on the codimension. -/
SIG 457: theorem exists_nested_spanning (H : Matrix S S ℂ) (U : G → Matrix S S ℂ) :
SIG 458:     ∀ (d : ℕ) (P : unitary (Matrix S S ℂ)), P ∈ posReach H U →
SIG 459:       ∀ W : Submodule ℝ (Matrix S S ℂ), W ≤ posSpan₀ H U →
SIG 460:         Module.finrank ℝ W + d = Module.finrank ℝ (posSpan₀ H U) →
SIG 461:         ∃ (n : ℕ) (A : Fin n → unitary (Matrix S S ℂ)), (∀ j, A j ∈ posReach H U) ∧
SIG 462:           W ⊔ Submodule.span ℝ (Set.range fun j => orbitDir H (P * prefixProd n A j))
SIG 463:             = posSpan₀ H U := by
