=== SpectatorBridge.lean:108 theorem mapSpectatorIndependent_iff_amplRef  HEADLINE
DOC 105: /-- **MAP-LEVEL SPECTATOR INDEPENDENCE IS REFERENCE AMPLIFICATION.** A composite map that
DOC 106: acts as `id_R ⊗ Φ` on every product input is `amplRefL R Φ` — composite matrix units are
DOC 107: products, so agreement on products is agreement everywhere. -/
SIG 108: theorem mapSpectatorIndependent_iff_amplRef (ΦB : Matrix S S ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix S S ℂ)
SIG 109:     (ΦRS : Matrix (R × S) (R × S) ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix (R × S) (R × S) ℂ) :
SIG 110:     MapSpectatorIndependent ΦB ΦRS ↔ ΦRS = amplRefL R ΦB := by
=== SpectatorBridge.lean:122 theorem spectatorIndependent_form  HEADLINE
DOC 120: /-- **THE SPECTATOR CLAUSE FIXES THE FORM.** Under spectator independence, the coherent
DOC 121: map assigned to `id_R × g` is exactly `id_R ⊗ (coherent map of g)`. -/
SIG 122: theorem spectatorIndependent_form (CB : Equiv.Perm S → Matrix S S ℂ)
SIG 123:     (C : Equiv.Perm (R × S) → Matrix (R × S) (R × S) ℂ) (h : SpectatorIndependent CB C)
SIG 124:     (g : Equiv.Perm S) :
SIG 125:     correlationExtension (spectatorExt g) (C (spectatorExt g))
SIG 126:       = amplRefL R (correlationExtension g (CB g)) :=
=== SpectatorBridge.lean:132 theorem hComp_spectator_form  HEADLINE
DOC 130: /-- **`H_comp` SUPPLIES THE FORM OF EVERY SPECTATOR EXTENSION IT NAMES** — the reversible
DOC 131: specialization of parallel reference extension, with `id_R ⊗ Φ` read off explicitly. -/
SIG 132: theorem hComp_spectator_form {ι : Type*} (act : ι → Equiv.Perm (R × S))
SIG 133:     (corr : ι → Matrix (R × S) (R × S) ℂ) (CB : Equiv.Perm S → Matrix S S ℂ)
SIG 134:     (C : Equiv.Perm (R × S) → Matrix (R × S) (R × S) ℂ) (h : HComp act corr CB C)
SIG 135:     (g : Equiv.Perm S) :
SIG 136:     correlationExtension (spectatorExt g) (C (spectatorExt g))
SIG 137:       = amplRefL R (correlationExtension g (CB g)) :=
=== SpectatorBridge.lean:150 theorem ext_of_agree_on_reindexed_single
DOC 148: /-- Two endomorphisms of the extended carrier agreeing on every reindexed matrix unit are
