SIG 150: theorem ext_of_agree_on_reindexed_single {n m : ℕ} (e : R × (A × Fin n) ≃ A × Fin m)
SIG 151:     (G G' : Matrix (A × Fin m) (A × Fin m) ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix (A × Fin m) (A × Fin m) ℂ)
SIG 152:     (h : ∀ p q : R × (A × Fin n),
SIG 153:       G (Matrix.reindex e e (Matrix.single p q 1)) = G' (Matrix.reindex e e (Matrix.single p q 1))) :
SIG 154:     G = G' := by
=== SpectatorBridge.lean:180 def IsSpectatorExtension  HEADLINE
DOC 176: /-- **A SPECTATOR EXTENSION, BY ITS ACTION.** `G` on the extended carrier is a spectator
DOC 177: extension of `Φ` along `e` when, on every reindexed product input `X_R ⊗ X`, it acts as
DOC 178: `X_R ⊗ Φ X`: it does what `Φ` does and leaves the spectator untouched. This is the
DOC 179: LOCALITY of an extension — its form — stated without presupposing existence. -/
SIG 180: def IsSpectatorExtension {n m : ℕ} (e : R × (A × Fin n) ≃ A × Fin m)
SIG 181:     (Φ : Matrix (A × Fin n) (A × Fin n) ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix (A × Fin n) (A × Fin n) ℂ)
SIG 182:     (G : Matrix (A × Fin m) (A × Fin m) ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix (A × Fin m) (A × Fin m) ℂ) : Prop :=
SIG 183:   ∀ (XR : Matrix R R ℂ) (X : Matrix (A × Fin n) (A × Fin n) ℂ),
SIG 184:     G (Matrix.reindex e e (tensorOf XR X)) = Matrix.reindex e e (tensorOf XR (Φ X))
=== SpectatorBridge.lean:188 theorem isSpectatorExtension_iff  HEADLINE
DOC 186: /-- **LOCALITY FIXES THE FORM UNIQUELY.** A spectator extension of `Φ` along `e` is
DOC 187: `withSpectator R e Φ`, and nothing else. -/
SIG 188: theorem isSpectatorExtension_iff {n m : ℕ} (e : R × (A × Fin n) ≃ A × Fin m)
SIG 189:     (Φ : Matrix (A × Fin n) (A × Fin n) ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix (A × Fin n) (A × Fin n) ℂ)
SIG 190:     (G : Matrix (A × Fin m) (A × Fin m) ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix (A × Fin m) (A × Fin m) ℂ) :
SIG 191:     IsSpectatorExtension e Φ G ↔ G = withSpectator R e Φ := by
=== SpectatorBridge.lean:202 theorem spectatorExtension_unique
DOC 201: /-- Two spectator extensions of the same map along the same reindexing coincide. -/
SIG 202: theorem spectatorExtension_unique {n m : ℕ} (e : R × (A × Fin n) ≃ A × Fin m)
SIG 203:     (Φ : Matrix (A × Fin n) (A × Fin n) ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix (A × Fin n) (A × Fin n) ℂ)
SIG 204:     {G G' : Matrix (A × Fin m) (A × Fin m) ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix (A × Fin m) (A × Fin m) ℂ}
SIG 205:     (hG : IsSpectatorExtension e Φ G) (hG' : IsSpectatorExtension e Φ G') : G = G' := by
=== SpectatorBridge.lean:223 def InertSpectatorCompositionality  HEADLINE
DOC 216: /-- **INERT-SPECTATOR COMPOSITIONALITY**, in physical words: an intervention performable on
DOC 217: a system remains performable when an independent finite spectator is adjoined, and acts
DOC 218: identically on that spectator. Formally: every available family at level `n` has, for
DOC 219: every finite spectator `R` and every relabelling `e` of the joint carrier into the
DOC 220: theory's carrier at level `m`, an AVAILABLE family at level `m` whose branches are
DOC 221: spectator extensions (in the sense of `IsSpectatorExtension`) of the original branches.
DOC 222: The definition asserts EXISTENCE of an available extension; its FORM is then forced. -/
SIG 223: def InertSpectatorCompositionality (T : FiniteOperationalTheory A) : Prop :=
SIG 224:   ∀ (R : Type) [Fintype R] [DecidableEq R] (n m : ℕ) (e : R × (A × Fin n) ≃ A × Fin m)
SIG 225:     (O : Type) [Fintype O] [DecidableEq O]
SIG 226:     (F : O → Matrix (A × Fin n) (A × Fin n) ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix (A × Fin n) (A × Fin n) ℂ),
SIG 227:     T.availExt n O F →
SIG 228:       ∃ G : O → Matrix (A × Fin m) (A × Fin m) ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix (A × Fin m) (A × Fin m) ℂ,
SIG 229:         T.availExt m O G ∧ ∀ a, IsSpectatorExtension e (F a) (G a)
=== SpectatorBridge.lean:233 theorem inertSpectator_iff_parallelReferenceExtension  HEADLINE
DOC 231: /-- **INERT-SPECTATOR COMPOSITIONALITY IS PARALLEL REFERENCE EXTENSION.** The existence
DOC 232: clause, once the form is forced, is exactly round thirty-five's property. -/
SIG 233: theorem inertSpectator_iff_parallelReferenceExtension (T : FiniteOperationalTheory A) :
SIG 234:     InertSpectatorCompositionality T ↔ HasParallelReferenceExtension T := by
