=== SpectatorBridge.lean:460 theorem hcompRealized_not_implies_parallelReferenceExtension  HEADLINE
DOC 455: /-- **`H_comp` REALIZED DOES NOT GIVE PARALLEL REFERENCE EXTENSION.** At the qutrit
DOC 456: spectator and the explicit reindexing of round thirty-five, with the full alphabet of
DOC 457: composite relabellings: `H_comp` holds, every coherent map it names is available, full
DOC 458: composite unitary control holds — and the theory refutes parallel reference extension,
DOC 459: hence inert-spectator compositionality. -/
SIG 460: theorem hcompRealized_not_implies_parallelReferenceExtension :
SIG 461:     ∃ T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2),
SIG 462:       HCompRealized T qutritIdx (id : Equiv.Perm (Fin 3 × (Fin 2 × Fin 2)) → _)
SIG 463:           (fun _ => onesCorr _) (fun _ => onesCorr _) (fun _ => onesCorr _)
SIG 464:         ∧ HasCompositeUnitaryControl T
SIG 465:         ∧ ¬ HasParallelReferenceExtension T ∧ ¬ InertSpectatorCompositionality T :=
=== SpectatorBridge.lean:472 theorem hcompRealized_consistent_with_parallelReferenceExtension  HEADLINE
DOC 469: /-- **THE SAME REALIZATION IS CONSISTENT WITH THE EXTENSION.** The full theory realizes the
DOC 470: same completion and has parallel reference extension: the realization decides neither way,
DOC 471: which is what "existence is an independent condition" means. -/
SIG 472: theorem hcompRealized_consistent_with_parallelReferenceExtension :
SIG 473:     ∃ T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2),
SIG 474:       HCompRealized T qutritIdx (id : Equiv.Perm (Fin 3 × (Fin 2 × Fin 2)) → _)
SIG 475:           (fun _ => onesCorr _) (fun _ => onesCorr _) (fun _ => onesCorr _)
SIG 476:         ∧ HasParallelReferenceExtension T ∧ InertSpectatorCompositionality T :=
