=== SecondOrderDrive.lean:480 theorem heis_eq_of_agree  HEADLINE
DOC 476: /-- **STABILIZATION AT THE SCAFFOLD LEVEL.** Two dynamics with the same effect on a region — the
DOC 477: same restricted configuration, and the same off-region agreement relation — have the same
DOC 478: Heisenberg action on that region's observables. This is what lets a layer over all sites be
DOC 479: replaced, on any one local observable, by a dynamics supported in a finite region. -/
SIG 480: theorem heis_eq_of_agree {Φ Ψ : ReversibleDynamics ι Q}
SIG 481:     (hglob : ∀ t : ι → Q, glob Λ (Φ.φ t) = glob Λ (Ψ.φ t))
SIG 482:     (hoff : ∀ t s : ι → Q, AgreeOffG Λ (Φ.φ t) (Φ.φ s) ↔ AgreeOffG Λ (Ψ.φ t) (Ψ.φ s))
SIG 483:     (X : Matrix (Conf Λ Q) (Conf Λ Q) ℂ) :
SIG 484:     heis Φ (emb Λ X) = heis Ψ (emb Λ X) := by
=== SecondOrderDrive.lean:502 def regionSwap
DOC 501: /-- The on-site exchange read on a whole region. -/
SIG 502: def regionSwap (V : Type) [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] [Nonempty V] [AddCommGroup V]
SIG 503:     (Λ : Finset ι) : Conf Λ (V × V) ≃ Conf Λ (V × V) where
SIG 504:   toFun f := fun u => ((f u).2, (f u).1)
SIG 505:   invFun f := fun u => ((f u).2, (f u).1)
SIG 506:   left_inv _ := rfl
SIG 507:   right_inv _ := rfl
