=== SecondOrderDrive.lean:519 theorem qGate_regionSwap_union  HEADLINE
DOC 517: /-- **THE REGION SWAPS COMPOSE.** Two disjoint regions' swaps multiply to the swap of their
DOC 518: union, which is what makes the finite gate product a single region's permutation matrix. -/
SIG 519: theorem qGate_regionSwap_union {Λ₁ Λ₂ : Finset ι} (hd : Disjoint Λ₁ Λ₂) :
SIG 520:     qGate Λ₁ (regionSwap V Λ₁) * qGate Λ₂ (regionSwap V Λ₂)
SIG 521:       = qGate (Λ₁ ∪ Λ₂) (regionSwap V (Λ₁ ∪ Λ₂)) := by
=== SecondOrderDrive.lean:545 theorem swapU_one_eq_qGate  HEADLINE
DOC 543: /-- **THE SWAP LAYER'S TIME-ONE UNITARY IS ONE REGION'S PERMUTATION MATRIX.** The finite product of
DOC 544: on-site gates over `Λ` is the permutation matrix of the swap of the whole of `Λ`. -/
SIG 545: theorem swapU_one_eq_qGate (Λ : Finset ι) :
SIG 546:     swapU V Λ 1 = qGate Λ (regionSwap V Λ) := by
