=== JordanClassification.lean:300 theorem proj_dyad_decomp
DOC 298: /-- A Hermitian idempotent is a partial sum of frame dyads: its eigenvalues are `0` or
DOC 299: `1`, so the spectral resolution truncates to the eigenvalue-one block. -/
SIG 300: theorem proj_dyad_decomp {p : Matrix n n ℂ} (hph : p.IsHermitian) (hp2 : p * p = p) :
SIG 301:     ∃ (U : Matrix n n ℂ) (S : Finset n), Uᴴ * U = 1 ∧ p = ∑ k ∈ S, edyad U k := by
=== JordanClassification.lean:336 theorem orthogonal_resolution_rank_one  HEADLINE
DOC 333: /-- **The rank-one resolution.** Nonzero pairwise-orthogonal Hermitian projections,
DOC 334: indexed by the dimension and summing to the identity, are dyads on an orthonormal frame:
DOC 335: the traces are naturals summing to `D` with `D` terms each at least one. -/
SIG 336: theorem orthogonal_resolution_rank_one (P : n → Matrix n n ℂ)
SIG 337:     (hh : ∀ i, (P i).IsHermitian) (hp2 : ∀ i, P i * P i = P i)
SIG 338:     (horth : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → P i * P j = 0)
SIG 339:     (hsum : ∑ i, P i = 1) (hne : ∀ i, P i ≠ 0) :
SIG 340:     ∃ v : n → n → ℂ,
SIG 341:       (∀ i j, star (v i) ⬝ᵥ v j = if i = j then 1 else 0)
SIG 342:       ∧ ∀ i, P i = Matrix.vecMulVec (v i) (star (v i)) := by
=== JordanClassification.lean:394 def qd
DOC 393: /-- The frame dyad `|v_i⟩⟨v_j|`. -/
SIG 394: def qd (v : n → n → ℂ) (i j : n) : Matrix n n ℂ :=
SIG 395:   Matrix.vecMulVec (v i) (star (v j))
