=== JordanClassification.lean:825 theorem matrixJordan_unitary_or_transpose  HEADLINE
DOC 818: /-- **THE MATRIX-UNIT CLASSIFICATION (C3b).** A ℂ-linear, unital, star-preserving,
DOC 819: injective Jordan homomorphism of `M_D(ℂ)` is conjugation by a unitary, or transpose
DOC 820: followed by conjugation by a unitary: `Φ(X) = WXW†` or `Φ(X) = WX^TW†`. The frame comes
DOC 821: from the rank-one resolution of the diagonal images, the orientation from triple
DOC 822: coherence, and the phases from the corner coboundary `α_ij = d_i · conj d_j` — the same
DOC 823: local-freedom → triple-consistency → global-orientation → phase-coboundary architecture
DOC 824: as the Hamiltonian reconstruction. -/
SIG 825: theorem matrixJordan_unitary_or_transpose
SIG 826:     (Φ : Matrix n n ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix n n ℂ)
SIG 827:     (hstar : ∀ X : Matrix n n ℂ, Φ Xᴴ = (Φ X)ᴴ)
SIG 828:     (hone : Φ 1 = 1) (hinj : Function.Injective Φ)
SIG 829:     (hj : ∀ A B : Matrix n n ℂ, Φ (A * B + B * A) = Φ A * Φ B + Φ B * Φ A) :
SIG 830:     ∃ W : Matrix n n ℂ, Wᴴ * W = 1 ∧
SIG 831:       ((∀ X, Φ X = W * X * Wᴴ) ∨ (∀ X, Φ X = W * Xᵀ * Wᴴ)) := by
=== JordanClassification.lean:951 theorem sameData_orderIso  HEADLINE
DOC 945: /-- **THE ASSEMBLY (C3b.3).** Two completions with identical pairing data, Hermitian
DOC 946: spanning contexts including the trivial one, separating accessible states, and full
DOC 947: accessible cones induce mutually inverse ℂ-linear maps matching every context — the
DOC 948: full two-sided order-isomorphism package. Bijectivity comes from the symmetric
DOC 949: operational construction, positivity from transfer + cone + self-duality, star
DOC 950: preservation by span induction over the Hermitian contexts. -/
SIG 951: theorem sameData_orderIso {ι κ : Type*}
SIG 952:     (G₁ G₂ : ι → Matrix n n ℂ) (σ₁ σ₂ : κ → Matrix n n ℂ)
SIG 953:     (hdata : ∀ i k, Matrix.trace (G₁ i * σ₁ k) = Matrix.trace (G₂ i * σ₂ k))
SIG 954:     (hG₁h : ∀ i, (G₁ i).IsHermitian) (hG₂h : ∀ i, (G₂ i).IsHermitian)
SIG 955:     (hσ₁p : ∀ k, (σ₁ k).PosSemidef) (hσ₂p : ∀ k, (σ₂ k).PosSemidef)
SIG 956:     (hspan₁ : Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range G₁) = ⊤)
SIG 957:     (hspan₂ : Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range G₂) = ⊤)
SIG 958:     (hsep₁ : ∀ M : Matrix n n ℂ, (∀ k, Matrix.trace (M * σ₁ k) = 0) → M = 0)
SIG 959:     (hsep₂ : ∀ M : Matrix n n ℂ, (∀ k, Matrix.trace (M * σ₂ k) = 0) → M = 0)
SIG 960:     (i₀ : ι) (hone₁ : G₁ i₀ = 1) (hone₂ : G₂ i₀ = 1)
SIG 961:     (hcone₁ : ∀ τ : Matrix n n ℂ, τ.PosSemidef → ∃ (s : Finset κ) (c : κ → ℝ),
SIG 962:       (∀ k, 0 ≤ c k) ∧ τ = ∑ k ∈ s, c k • σ₁ k)
SIG 963:     (hcone₂ : ∀ τ : Matrix n n ℂ, τ.PosSemidef → ∃ (s : Finset κ) (c : κ → ℝ),
SIG 964:       (∀ k, 0 ≤ c k) ∧ τ = ∑ k ∈ s, c k • σ₂ k) :
SIG 965:     ∃ Φ Ψ : Matrix n n ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix n n ℂ,
SIG 966:       (∀ i, Φ (G₁ i) = G₂ i) ∧ (∀ i, Ψ (G₂ i) = G₁ i)
SIG 967:         ∧ OrderIsoHyp (⇑Φ) (⇑Ψ) := by
=== JordanClassification.lean:1109 theorem sameData_unitary_or_transpose  HEADLINE
DOC 1103: /-- **THE C3b CLASSIFICATION.** Any two existing OI-compatible coherent completions with
DOC 1104: the same complete operational data are unitary or antiunitary equivalent: the
DOC 1105: data-defined map exists, is a two-sided order isomorphism, hence Jordan (round six),
DOC 1106: hence — by the matrix-unit classification — conjugation by a unitary `W`, directly or
DOC 1107: through the transpose. Which branch is physical is C3c: phase two's oriented complex
DOC 1108: reference is the lever that removes the transpose. -/
