=== OperationalRigidity.lean:129 theorem conj_context_entry  HEADLINE
DOC 126: /-- **The s-conjugated context entry, frequency-resolved**: sandwiching a one-slot
DOC 127: context times the operator between `V†…V` expands each entry as a line of gap
DOC 128: characters — the input to the second extraction. -/
SIG 129: theorem conj_context_entry {n : Type*} [Fintype n] (V : Matrix n (Fin Dm) ℂ)
SIG 130:     (hV' : Vᴴ * V = 1) (E : Fin Dm → ℝ) (B X : Matrix n n ℂ) (s : ℝ) (x y : Fin Dm) :
SIG 131:     (Vᴴ * (Matrix.of (BohrFrequency.Umat V E s) * B
SIG 132:         * (Matrix.of (BohrFrequency.Umat V E s))ᴴ * X) * V) x y
SIG 133:       = ∑ c, (Vᴴ * B * V) x c * (Vᴴ * X * V) c y
SIG 134:           * Complex.exp (Complex.I * ((E c - E x : ℝ) : ℂ) * (s : ℂ)) := by
=== OperationalRigidity.lean:170 theorem operational_separation  HEADLINE
DOC 163: /-- **OPERATIONAL SEPARATION (C3b.1).** An operator invisible to the normalization
DOC 164: datum, every one-slot context, and every two-slot context is ZERO. The one-slot layer
DOC 165: kills the off-diagonal of `Y = V† X V` (round five's extraction); the two-slot layer
DOC 166: reduces, through the same extraction, to a line of gap characters in the second time,
DOC 167: whose coefficients kill the diagonal. Probe F18: one-slot data alone do NOT suffice —
DOC 168: the census carrier admits two distinct exact states with identical one-slot data —
DOC 169: so the two-slot hypothesis is load-bearing, not convenience. -/
SIG 170: theorem operational_separation {n ι' : Type*} [Fintype n] [DecidableEq n]
SIG 171:     (V : Matrix n (Fin Dm) ℂ) (E : Fin Dm → ℝ) (A : ι' → Matrix n n ℂ)
SIG 172:     (X : Matrix n n ℂ) (hV : V * Vᴴ = 1) (hV' : Vᴴ * V = 1)
SIG 173:     (hgap : ∀ a b c d : Fin Dm, a ≠ b → c ≠ d → E b - E a = E d - E c → a = c ∧ b = d)
SIG 174:     (hcomplete : ∀ a b : Fin Dm, a ≠ b → ∃ j, (Vᴴ * A j * V) a b ≠ 0)
SIG 175:     (htr : Matrix.trace X = 0)
SIG 176:     (h1 : ∀ (j : ι') (t : ℝ),
SIG 177:       Matrix.trace (Matrix.of (BohrFrequency.Umat V E t) * A j
SIG 178:         * (Matrix.of (BohrFrequency.Umat V E t))ᴴ * X) = 0)
SIG 179:     (h2 : ∀ (j k : ι') (t s : ℝ),
SIG 180:       Matrix.trace (Matrix.of (BohrFrequency.Umat V E t) * A j
SIG 181:         * (Matrix.of (BohrFrequency.Umat V E t))ᴴ
SIG 182:         * (Matrix.of (BohrFrequency.Umat V E s) * A k
SIG 183:           * (Matrix.of (BohrFrequency.Umat V E s))ᴴ * X)) = 0) :
SIG 184:     X = 0 := by
=== OperationalRigidity.lean:256 theorem sameData_unique_state  HEADLINE
DOC 253: /-- **State-side rigidity**: two preparations carrying identical normalization,
