DOC 713: /-- **Order isomorphisms transport projections** (extreme points of the operator
DOC 714: interval map to extreme points, and those are exactly the projections). -/
SIG 715: theorem orderIso_maps_projections {Φ Ψ : Matrix n n ℂ → Matrix n n ℂ}
SIG 716:     (h : OrderIsoHyp Φ Ψ) {P : Matrix n n ℂ}
SIG 717:     (hPh : P.IsHermitian) (hP2 : P * P = P) :
SIG 718:     (Φ P).IsHermitian ∧ Φ P * Φ P = Φ P := by
=== OperationalRigidity.lean:756 theorem orderIso_orthogonal  HEADLINE
DOC 753: /-- **Order isomorphisms transport orthogonality** of projections: additivity plus the
DOC 754: projection transport force the anticommutator to vanish, and the projection algebra
DOC 755: turns that into a vanishing product. -/
SIG 756: theorem orderIso_orthogonal {Φ Ψ : Matrix n n ℂ → Matrix n n ℂ}
SIG 757:     (h : OrderIsoHyp Φ Ψ) {P Q : Matrix n n ℂ}
SIG 758:     (hPh : P.IsHermitian) (hQh : Q.IsHermitian)
SIG 759:     (hP2 : P * P = P) (hQ2 : Q * Q = Q)
SIG 760:     (hPQ : P * Q = 0) (hQP : Q * P = 0) :
SIG 761:     Φ P * Φ Q = 0 := by
=== OperationalRigidity.lean:796 theorem orderIso_square  HEADLINE
DOC 793: /-- **The square is preserved** (`Φ(A²) = Φ(A)²` on Hermitians): resolve `A` into its
DOC 794: rank-one eigenframe dyads; their images are pairwise-orthogonal projections, so both
DOC 795: squares recombine to the same eigenvalue-squared resolution. -/
SIG 796: theorem orderIso_square {Φ Ψ : Matrix n n ℂ → Matrix n n ℂ}
SIG 797:     (h : OrderIsoHyp Φ Ψ) {A : Matrix n n ℂ} (hAh : A.IsHermitian) :
SIG 798:     Φ (A * A) = Φ A * Φ A := by
=== OperationalRigidity.lean:848 theorem orderIso_jordan  HEADLINE
DOC 845: /-- **THE KADISON THEOREM, kernel-internal (C3b.2).** A unital ℝ-linear star-preserving
DOC 846: bijection of `M_D(ℂ)` that is positive in both directions is a Jordan ∗-isomorphism on
DOC 847: Hermitians: `Φ(AB + BA) = Φ(A)Φ(B) + Φ(B)Φ(A)`. Polarization of `orderIso_square`. -/
SIG 848: theorem orderIso_jordan {Φ Ψ : Matrix n n ℂ → Matrix n n ℂ}
SIG 849:     (h : OrderIsoHyp Φ Ψ) {A B : Matrix n n ℂ}
SIG 850:     (hAh : A.IsHermitian) (hBh : B.IsHermitian) :
SIG 851:     Φ (A * B + B * A) = Φ A * Φ B + Φ B * Φ A := by
