=== PassiveIndependence.lean:269 theorem passive_nondiscriminating  HEADLINE
DOC 265: /-- **OI-N4, the diagram.** Passive incompleteness holds in every theory on the qubit; the OI
DOC 266: core holds in some (`diagTheory`) and fails in others (`labelTheory`). Passive incompleteness is
DOC 267: theory-insensitive, so it carries no discriminatory information about whether the OI core is
DOC 268: realized: the forward implication is vacuous and the converse fails. -/
SIG 269: theorem passive_nondiscriminating :
SIG 270:     (∀ T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2), PassivelyIncomplete T)
SIG 271:     ∧ (∃ T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2), OICore T ∧ PassivelyIncomplete T)
SIG 272:     ∧ (∃ T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2), ¬ OICore T ∧ PassivelyIncomplete T) :=
=== PassiveIndependence.lean:288 def PassivelyCompleteOnDiagonal  HEADLINE
DOC 285: /-- **Passive completeness on the commutative sector**: some available family is completely
DOC 286: positive, fixes every diagonal matrix nonselectively, and separates diagonal matrices by outcome
DOC 287: law. -/
SIG 288: def PassivelyCompleteOnDiagonal (T : FiniteOperationalTheory A) : Prop :=
SIG 289:   ∃ (O : Type) (_ : Fintype O) (_ : DecidableEq O) (F : O → Matrix A A ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix A A ℂ),
SIG 290:     T.avail O F ∧ (∀ a, IsCompletelyPositive (F a)) ∧ (∀ X, IsDiagonal X → ∑ a, (F a) X = X)
SIG 291:     ∧ ∀ ρ σ : Matrix A A ℂ, IsDiagonal ρ → IsDiagonal σ →
SIG 292:         (∀ a, ((F a) ρ).trace = ((F a) σ).trace) → ρ = σ
